          "body": "Operator clients previously lost their session on daemon restart and could not safely reconcile a submission after losing its response. The CLI also printed credentials, and composed operator views could mix different ledger snapshots.\n\nThis adds durable operator sessions and revocation, private bootstrap/credential files, operator-owned command discovery, exact journaled retries returning the original command's current phase, and authenticated atomic snapshots. The Rust CLI uses generated models and bounded response validation; the new read-only Ratatui console preserves selection and detaches without stopping work. Append-only migrations preserve historical commands without assigning them an inferred owner.\n\nThe matching Portal changes are neverhuman/bullet-portal#5 and its follow-up #6. This remains a component milestone: task-shaped server allocation, scheduling, native lifecycle controls, independent completion and persistent installation remain open. Operating HOLD remains effective.\n\nValidation:\n- Focused CLI: 45 unit tests, two authentication PTY tests and one TUI PTY test passed.\n- Durable command ownership/recovery packet: 85 focused tests passed.\n- Inventory: 1,237 identities accounted for as 1,191 standalone + 34 provider contract + 3 egress + 9 family; enumeration is distinct from execution.\n- Generated-contract, formatting, offline-wrapper guard and hosted-workflow policy checks passed.\n- Full local required passed on f0f1bdcb9c894b49674276b2050d754de8829368: 1,191 standalone and 34 contract tests, plus lint, security and docs.\n- Both current GitHub push/PR runs passed all seven required jobs: [push](https://github.com/neverhuman/bullet-kernel/actions/runs/34432421408) and [PR](https://github.com/neverhuman/bullet-kernel/actions/runs/34432424660).\n- Native provider execution, the family/egress lanes and persistent installation are not covered by these results.\n- Previous hosted failures are retained. This source installs the missing lint-job scanner and locked b3sum dependency; no required checks are suppressed.\n",
          "reactions": {
